<article class="env-lemma" id="055V">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/055V">Lemma <span data-tag="055V">37.38.7</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $\mathcal{U} = \{ S_ i \to S\} _{i \in I}$ be a smooth covering of $S$, see Topologies, Definition <a href="/tag/021Z" data-tag="021Z">34.5.1</a>. Then there exists an étale covering $\mathcal{V} = \{ T_ j \to S\} _{j \in J}$ (see Topologies, Definition <a href="/tag/0215" data-tag="0215">34.4.1</a>) which refines (see Sites, Definition <a href="/tag/00VT" data-tag="00VT">7.8.1</a>) $\mathcal{U}$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      For every $s \in S$ there exists an $i \in I$ such that $s$ is in the image of $S_ i \to S$. By Lemma <a href="/tag/055U" data-tag="055U">37.38.6</a> we can find an étale morphism $g_ s : T_ s \to S$ such that $s \in g_ s(T_ s)$ and such that $g_ s$ factors through $S_ i \to S$. Hence $\{ T_ s \to S\} $ is an étale covering of $S$ that refines $\mathcal{U}$. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>